(b) Codes which are to be enforced by building official. The rules, regulations, codes, or standards heretofore adopted, together with those state minimum standard codes enumerated in subdivision (9)(B)(i)(I) through (VIII) of section 8-2-20 of the Official Code of Georgia Annotated:
(1) International Building Code (IBC), with Georgia amendments;
(2) National Electrical Code, with Georgia amendments;
(3) International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC), with Georgia amendments;
(4) International Mechanical Code (IMC), with Georgia amendments;
(5) International Plumbing Code (IPC), with Georgia amendments;
(6) International Residential Code (IRC) for One- and Two-Family Dwelling, with Georgia amendments, specifically excluding section(s), entitled Smoke Detectors.
The following regulations pertaining to smoke detectors, previously contained in the IRC One- and Two-Family Dwelling Code, and new regulations pertaining to residential sprinklers are hereby adopted:
Smoke detectors required. Smoke detectors shall be installed in every sleeping room, outside of each separate sleeping area in the immediate vicinity of the bedrooms and on each additional story of the dwelling, including basements and cellars but not including crawl spaces and uninhabitable attics. In dwellings or dwelling units with split levels, a smoke detector need be installed only on the upper level, provided the lower level is less than one full story below the upper level, except that if there is a door between levels, then a detector is required on each level. All detectors shall be interconnected such that the actuation of one alarm will actuate all the alarms in the individual unit and shall provide an alarm which will be audible in all sleeping areas. All detectors shall be approved and listed and shall be installed in accordance with the manufacturer's instructions.
Residential fire sprinklers required. An automatic fire sprinkler system shall be installed in all new one- and two-family dwellings regardless of the type of construction. The system shall conform to the NFPA 13D, 2006 Edition, Standard for the Installation of Sprinkler Systems in One- and Two-Family Dwellings and Manufactured Homes. Modifications: None.
Reference: Rules of the Safety Fire Commissioner State Minimum Fire Safety Standards, 120-3-3.04.
(7) International Energy Conservation Code (IECC), with Georgia supplements and amendments;
(8) International Fire Code (IFC), with Georgia amendments;
(9) National Green Building Standards (NGBS), with Georgia amendments.
Codes which have statewide application and do not require adoption by local ordinance, shall be enforced by the building official or his designee(s) in accordance with the procedures hereinafter set forth.
The edition of such codes as currently adopted by the Georgia Department of Community Affairs shall be used and enforced, except where a subsequently published edition of any such code has been adopted by the Georgia Department of Community Affairs, with approval of its board, or such code has been amended or revised as provided in section 8-2-23 of the Official Code of Georgia Annotated.
(c) Application, interpretation and enforcement of IECC. Except in regard to buildings owned by the State of Georgia, the design, erection, construction and alteration of any building to which the IECC for Buildings, with Georgia amendments, shall apply shall be accomplished so that the building or applicable portions thereof shall meet or conform to such code. The IECC for Buildings shall not apply to exempted buildings; and, with respect to renovated buildings, such code shall apply only to portions or systems of the building which are directly involved in the renovation. Interpretation and enforcement of such code shall be solely within the province of the building official; provided, however, the commissioner of the Department of Community Affairs or his designated representative shall hear appeals relating to the interpretation, enforcement and administration of such code and may remand any case to the city with instructions to take such action as he directs.
(d) Availability of codes; public inspection and copying. Copies of the current edition of all applicable codes shall be maintained in the building official's office at City Hall for public inspection and copying during regular business hours.
(Ord. No. 98-02, § 1, 6-23-98; Ord. No. 99-11, § 3, 4-27-99; Ord. No. 2001-01, § 1, 1-23-01; Ord. No. 2001-22, §§ 1, 2, 12-11-01; Ord. No. 2003-03, § 1(A), (B), 1-28-03; Ord. No. 2007-01, 1-23-07; Ord. No. 2014-02, 4-22-14; Ord. No. 2018-02, 2-13-18)

373:
(a) The building official, and his designated representatives, shall have and exercise the following duties and responsibilities in the enforcement of state minimum standard codes:
(1) To interpret, enforce, and administer the state minimum standard codes within the city in accordance with the provisions and procedural requirements of this chapter;
(2) To inspect all existing buildings and structures as required by such codes and to permit and inspect new construction and the renovation, alteration, modification and repairs to existing structures to assure compliance with applicable state minimum code standards;
